# the devthink family build context (the flat village era container law):
# THE Dockerfile of the devthink application builds from the repository
# root, because the application tree alone no longer carries everything
# the build needs — the dependency union pins the vault sibling in the
# manifest ("@wenathlan/vault": "file:../vault"), the flat test village
# (tests/) owns the build engine and the vitest suite the builder runs,
# and the config bridges resolve the getry ladder and the saddle sandbox
# onto their sibling owner sources. this ignore keeps the junk out of the
# context tarball at every depth: the git history, the local installs,
# the built trees, the release scratch and the ephemeral worktrees never
# enter a build. the tracked evidence zips under devthink/docs stay in
# (the archives this file excludes are the untracked release scratch that
# lands beside the manifests of the application trees).
.git
.worktrees
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/distpackage
**/build
**/release
**/staging
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
devthink/.manus-logs
devthink/mobile
devthink/tests/tmp
tests/tmp
devthink/.env
devthink/.env.*
devthink/*.log
devthink/*.sqlite
devthink/*.db
devthink/*.tgz
devthink/*.zip
devthink/*.xpi
devthink/*.vsix
devthink/*.tar.gz
